139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111348 1068 #edb/ref 17592186109783 13194139533425 17592186045585 false] [17592186111348 1068 #edb/ref 17592186335358 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111348 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111348 1071 "![](images/96/96b22799c75a4b19df4c6bddf8b63d11a7d0cab8a0cc481b8466a29eb1a2af15.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}$, use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\tan θ$." 13194139533425 17592186045585 false] [17592186111348 1071 "![](images/96/96b22799c75a4b19df4c6bddf8b63d11a7d0cab8a0cc481b8466a29eb1a2af15.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7},$ use the Pythagorean identity to find $tan⁡\\theta .$" 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111348 1074 "![](images/21/21170c11aa5ff0ab39b86f94588e5e8a0fa178d0c34b9aa1774ee9f07a4d0812.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=cos⁡\\theta ,\\,y=sin⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nsin⁡\\theta =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{45}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the positive answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7})}{(\\frac{2}{7})}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111358 1068 #edb/ref 17592186109843 13194139533425 17592186045585 false] [17592186111358 1068 #edb/ref 17592186335693 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111358 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111358 1071 "${sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x=$" 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111358 1071 "What is $\\sec^{2} x - 2\\tan^{2} x$?" 13194139533425 17592186045585 false] [17592186111358 1074 "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x & =1+{tan}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x=1-{tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111359 1068 #edb/ref 17592186109849 13194139533425 17592186045585 false] [17592186111359 1068 #edb/ref 17592186335687 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111359 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111359 1071 "Simplify $\\frac{\\cot θ}{\\csc^{2} θ - 1}$." 13194139533425 17592186045585 false] [17592186111359 1071 "Simplify $\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}.$" 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111359 1074 "First, let's recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={cot}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533425 17592186045585 true] [17592186111363 1068 #edb/ref 17592186109873 13194139533425 1759218604558